WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:02.234
-Ah, I'm so happy you're here.

00:00:02.234 --> 00:00:04.901
-I'm so happy I'm here, too.
-I'm so happy.

00:00:04.901 --> 00:00:07.300
I'm the biggest fan.
I love that you're here.

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:09.601
Congrats on "SNL."
That's going to be fun.

00:00:09.601 --> 00:00:11.000
-Yeah.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.634
-This is your first
U.S. talk show.

00:00:13.634 --> 00:00:15.133
-It is.
-Yes.

00:00:15.133 --> 00:00:17.334
-I know --
-Thank you for choosing us.

00:00:17.334 --> 00:00:19.000
Thank you for choosing me.
I appreciate it.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:20.467
-What? I'm a huge fan.

00:00:20.467 --> 00:00:21.968
I wanted to come,
like, since forever.

00:00:21.968 --> 00:00:23.167
I've seen the videos.

00:00:23.167 --> 00:00:24.400
-Yeah.
-Your videos.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:26.234
I thought it was on Instagram
or YouTube.

00:00:26.234 --> 00:00:29.067
And I'm always like, "I really
want to talk with him."

00:00:29.067 --> 00:00:30.534
-Oh, no, I'm so happy.

00:00:30.534 --> 00:00:32.801
And I just want to make sure
I'm saying your name right.

00:00:32.801 --> 00:00:34.834
-Okay.
-Rosalía.

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:36.334
-Not bad.
-Oh.

00:00:36.334 --> 00:00:37.868
[ Laughter ]
-No, really.

00:00:37.868 --> 00:00:39.334
No. Actually not bad.
-Okay.

00:00:39.334 --> 00:00:41.467
-Because, usually,
people I see here, they --

00:00:41.467 --> 00:00:44.367
you don't really r-r-roll
the R's so much, no?

00:00:44.367 --> 00:00:46.734
-Wow.
You just really r-rolled --

00:00:46.734 --> 00:00:48.968
-Like -- Yeah. R-R-Rosalía.

00:00:48.968 --> 00:00:52.133
-Ooh. R-R-Rosalía.

00:00:52.133 --> 00:00:53.400
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:55.601
-Like that? Like that?
-Yeah!

00:00:55.601 --> 00:00:58.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:00.868
-Wasn't bad. That wasn't bad.
I've heard so many options.

00:01:00.868 --> 00:01:04.501
Like -- Rosalina.
-Rosalita.

00:01:04.501 --> 00:01:06.033
-Rosalita. But --

00:01:06.033 --> 00:01:08.334
Yeah, it's usually,
like, Rosalina...

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:10.234
-Rosalina.
-Rowzalia.

00:01:10.234 --> 00:01:13.200
-Rowzalia. Rosalía.
-Thank you.

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:15.167
-Thank you.
That's it right there. Yes.

00:01:15.167 --> 00:01:18.868
Welcome. You are --

00:01:18.868 --> 00:01:21.701
You started
as a flamenco singer.

00:01:21.701 --> 00:01:24.901
But your music today
is made up of so many genres.

00:01:24.901 --> 00:01:28.067
You've kind of destroyed
out there, in the market.

00:01:28.067 --> 00:01:29.968
You've won eight Latin Grammys.

00:01:29.968 --> 00:01:31.934
[ Cheers and applause ]
Hello.

00:01:31.934 --> 00:01:35.033
Not too shabby. Not bad.

00:01:35.033 --> 00:01:36.133
-It happened. It happened.

00:01:36.133 --> 00:01:38.234
-Yeah, and then here it is
right here.

00:01:38.234 --> 00:01:40.834
"Motomami" is coming out
March 18th.

00:01:40.834 --> 00:01:42.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:42.234 --> 00:01:43.934
-Yes!
-I love the drawing.

00:01:43.934 --> 00:01:46.734
I love the way it looks.
I love -- Why is it called --

00:01:46.734 --> 00:01:48.367
Would I know
what "Motomami" means?

00:01:48.367 --> 00:01:50.300
-Mm-hmm.
-I would?

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:52.767
-Okay, so, you want to know
why it's called "Motomami"?

00:01:52.767 --> 00:01:54.100
-Yeah.

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:55.601
-'Cause I feel like
Motomami's an energy.

00:01:55.601 --> 00:01:57.968
-Oh. I like that.
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:57.968 --> 00:01:59.534
Yes, yes. It's like an energy.

00:01:59.534 --> 00:02:01.534
-Now, I'm feeling it, yeah.
I'm feeling the Motomami energy.

00:02:01.534 --> 00:02:03.601
-That's what I'm saying.
Okay, so --

00:02:03.601 --> 00:02:06.300
Maybe -- Probably
you're a Motopapi, too.

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:08.133
-Yeah. Oh, my gosh.

00:02:08.133 --> 00:02:11.667
I would totally be -- Yeah.
I'm totally a Motopapi.

00:02:11.667 --> 00:02:14.634
-Yeah.
-I am so Moto --

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:15.934
Everyone share that.
That's going to be my nickname.

00:02:15.934 --> 00:02:17.167
-How do you know
that you're a Motopapi, though?

00:02:17.167 --> 00:02:20.267
-Because I can --
I can just feel it.

00:02:20.267 --> 00:02:23.701
Once I --
Once I r-r-rolled the R's,

00:02:23.701 --> 00:02:25.234
I knew that I was --
-You're like,

00:02:25.234 --> 00:02:26.868
"Yeah, I'm Motopapi."
-I'm Motopapi.

00:02:26.868 --> 00:02:29.901
Come on. Yeah.
I can really feel it.

00:02:29.901 --> 00:02:31.667
Motomami and Motopapi.

00:02:31.667 --> 00:02:33.400
-Yeah, that's what I'm saying.

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:35.434
-You know, I wanted
to ask you this question

00:02:35.434 --> 00:02:38.434
because it's --
it has a funny ending.

00:02:38.434 --> 00:02:40.000
We were talking backstage.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:41.501
I was going to say, "Hey,
I heard that you change

00:02:41.501 --> 00:02:43.968
your phone number a lot."

00:02:43.968 --> 00:02:45.501
You do?
Me -- I used to, too.

00:02:45.501 --> 00:02:47.501
-I change it so often.

00:02:47.501 --> 00:02:48.734
Before, I used to do it a lot.

00:02:48.734 --> 00:02:50.167
-Because too many people
just get your number

00:02:50.167 --> 00:02:52.601
and start calling you.
Is that why?

00:02:52.601 --> 00:02:55.501
-No, because I didn't
answer the messages.

00:02:55.501 --> 00:02:56.968
And then I realized, you know,

00:02:56.968 --> 00:02:59.801
that I wanted to focus
beyond the studio and work.

00:02:59.801 --> 00:03:01.968
-Ah.
-And now I wanted to focus.

00:03:01.968 --> 00:03:04.334
-Yeah, me too.
I wanted to focus, too.

00:03:04.334 --> 00:03:06.467
Focus on work.
That's why I changed my number.

00:03:06.467 --> 00:03:08.000
Yeah.
-No, I mean it.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:10.667
And then I was like,
"Okay. Mira. I'd rather not."

00:03:10.667 --> 00:03:13.000
Change the phone. Fresh start.
-Yeah.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:14.701
-You know?
-Yeah.

00:03:14.701 --> 00:03:17.400
And then what happens is you --
you change your number.

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:21.100
But then people text -- Because
someone else gets that number.

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:23.567
And then your friends
starts texting that number,

00:03:23.567 --> 00:03:25.200
not knowing
that you changed yours.

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:26.968
-That happen to you?
'Cause that happened to me.

00:03:26.968 --> 00:03:28.567
-Yeah, it does.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.567 --> 00:03:31.334
-I mean it. That happened to me.
Like, literally, I realized --

00:03:31.334 --> 00:03:33.000
'Cause I didn't know
that that happened.

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:36.868
I thought when you use a phone
number, then the phone number --

00:03:36.868 --> 00:03:38.234
you know, like, disappears
or something.

00:03:38.234 --> 00:03:40.901
I don't know why I thought that.
-Yeah, that should happen.

00:03:40.901 --> 00:03:42.868
They should, like, at least wait
a couple of years and then --

00:03:42.868 --> 00:03:44.234
-It was your number.

00:03:44.234 --> 00:03:46.834
-If it's your number,
at least wait -- Thank you.

00:03:46.834 --> 00:03:48.667
If it's your number --

00:03:48.667 --> 00:03:50.467
I mean, I'm Motopapi.
I don't mess around.

00:03:50.467 --> 00:03:52.634
I go, if you want
to take my number --

00:03:52.634 --> 00:03:54.234
If I change it, it should be --

00:03:54.234 --> 00:03:56.434
-Period.
-Out. For at least ten years.

00:03:56.434 --> 00:03:58.000
-But that doesn't happen.
-No.

00:03:58.000 --> 00:03:59.968
-And then I realized
that people --

00:03:59.968 --> 00:04:02.567
My friends thought
that they were texting me.

00:04:02.567 --> 00:04:04.434
They were texting random people.

00:04:04.434 --> 00:04:06.667
-But that happened to you --
For a friend that we know,

00:04:06.667 --> 00:04:08.234
as well,
that's been on our show.

00:04:08.234 --> 00:04:10.868
Harry Styles.
-Yeah. That happened.

00:04:10.868 --> 00:04:13.701
[ Laughs ] That happened.

00:04:13.701 --> 00:04:16.834
-So, talk to me.
So, Harry texts you.

00:04:16.834 --> 00:04:18.901
-I have proof.
Like, it happened.

00:04:18.901 --> 00:04:20.767
-You have proof?

00:04:20.767 --> 00:04:22.567
Like, what do you have?
A photo? What do you have?

00:04:22.567 --> 00:04:24.434
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.434 --> 00:04:26.501
-I literally have proof.

00:04:26.501 --> 00:04:29.200
[ Laughter ]

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:32.868
-Where -- Yeah, no. No problem.
-Okay.

00:04:32.868 --> 00:04:34.634
-What are you doing?

00:04:34.634 --> 00:04:37.701
Wait. You had your phone
in your boot?

00:04:37.701 --> 00:04:39.467
[ Laughter ]
-Yes.

00:04:39.467 --> 00:04:41.167
-That's where you keep
your phone?

00:04:41.167 --> 00:04:43.534
[ Cheers and applause ]
That's so cool.

00:04:43.534 --> 00:04:45.033
I'm going to start
doing that, too.

00:04:45.033 --> 00:04:46.267
Are you kidding me?

00:04:46.267 --> 00:04:47.767
I'm gonna totally keep
my phone in my...

00:04:47.767 --> 00:04:49.067
-I'm Motomami.

00:04:49.067 --> 00:04:51.934
Even Motomami needs to keep
the phone in the boot.

00:04:51.934 --> 00:04:53.334
She keep it in the boot.
-Yes.

00:04:53.334 --> 00:04:55.100
-It's perfect
to match the outfit.

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:57.033
It's, like, in the boot.

00:04:57.033 --> 00:04:58.601
-Yes.
-You know what I mean?

00:04:58.601 --> 00:04:59.934
-It's in the boot, man, yeah.

00:04:59.934 --> 00:05:02.534
All right, so you --
-You want to see?

00:05:02.534 --> 00:05:03.934
-I really do.

00:05:03.934 --> 00:05:07.501
This is a real -- Now,
how did you end up with this?

00:05:07.501 --> 00:05:09.801
So, Harry Styles texts you,
thinking it's you.

00:05:09.801 --> 00:05:12.167
But it's not. Someone else
has the phone number.

00:05:12.167 --> 00:05:13.601
-Yeah.
-And this is real.

00:05:13.601 --> 00:05:15.634
-Look, look. Okay, look.

00:05:15.634 --> 00:05:16.701
Okay.

00:05:16.701 --> 00:05:18.634
-All right. Let me -- All right.

00:05:18.634 --> 00:05:20.400
-Can't you believe he thought --
-So, which one is he?

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:22.834
-He sent me.
It's a screenshot, okay.

00:05:22.834 --> 00:05:24.934
In the DMs, in Instagram DMs.
-Yeah.

00:05:24.934 --> 00:05:27.701
-Saying, "Your texts
are confusing."

00:05:27.701 --> 00:05:29.701
-That was Harry that said,
"This is so beautiful"?

00:05:29.701 --> 00:05:30.901
-Yeah, he said that.

00:05:30.901 --> 00:05:32.567
Because he was like,
"Oh, I love this song."

00:05:32.567 --> 00:05:34.367
That is called "Dolerme."
-Yes.

00:05:34.367 --> 00:05:35.567
-He sent me --
there's a screenshot --

00:05:35.567 --> 00:05:37.634
that he was like --
-"This is beautiful."

00:05:37.634 --> 00:05:40.667
And then you wrote back --
or supposedly you wrote back.

00:05:40.667 --> 00:05:42.501
-And it wasn't me.

00:05:42.501 --> 00:05:44.300
[ Laughter ]
-"I know, my darling."

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:46.801
-The random person said, yeah,
"I know, my darling."

00:05:46.801 --> 00:05:49.167
-And then he says, "Love it."

00:05:49.167 --> 00:05:50.801
-And then he says...

00:05:50.801 --> 00:05:54.400
[ Laughter ]
..."Love you."

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:56.734
-"Love you."
And then Harry says...

00:05:56.734 --> 00:05:58.834
"I love you too."

00:05:58.834 --> 00:06:02.100
With lots of O's.
Very romantic. Very --

00:06:02.100 --> 00:06:05.734
And then this person writes...
-The person says, "Haha sorry.

00:06:05.734 --> 00:06:08.334
You're wrong.
I don't know who you are."

00:06:08.334 --> 00:06:09.634
[ Laughter ]

00:06:09.634 --> 00:06:12.200
-And then --
And then Harry writes back,

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:13.367
"I'm confused."

00:06:13.367 --> 00:06:15.934
[ Laughter ]

00:06:15.934 --> 00:06:18.400
And then the person puts --
-The person -- Oh, my God.

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:21.667
The person says, "This number
belongs to someone before.

00:06:21.667 --> 00:06:26.167
But now it's my number.
So don't bother me anymore.

00:06:26.167 --> 00:06:28.501
Good night. Thank you."

00:06:28.501 --> 00:06:31.033
[ Applause ]

00:06:31.033 --> 00:06:35.334
♪♪

00:06:35.334 --> 00:06:37.367
-To Harry --

00:06:37.367 --> 00:06:39.133
Dude.

00:06:39.133 --> 00:06:41.334
-Imagine -- Imagine --
-To Harry Styles.

00:06:41.334 --> 00:06:43.434
-Imagine being that person
now looking

00:06:43.434 --> 00:06:45.901
to the "Jimmy Fallon" show
and say,

00:06:45.901 --> 00:06:48.901
"I said, 'Don't bother me
anymore,' to Harry Styles!"

00:06:48.901 --> 00:06:51.767
[ Laughter ]

00:06:51.767 --> 00:06:53.734
-So, Harry just sent it
in your DM and was like,

00:06:53.734 --> 00:06:55.000
"Hey, what's going on with you?"

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:57.567
-So he said, "These --
These texts are confusing.

00:06:57.567 --> 00:06:59.567
Your texts are confusing."
He says something like that.

00:06:59.567 --> 00:07:01.167
And I was like,
"Wait. What do you mean?"

00:07:01.167 --> 00:07:02.834
-That's an old number.
Oh, my God.

00:07:02.834 --> 00:07:04.767
-And then I realize --
-That is the best thing ever.

00:07:04.767 --> 00:07:06.067
-No.
-All right.

00:07:06.067 --> 00:07:08.334
Save it.
Protect it in your boot forever.

00:07:08.334 --> 00:07:09.567
[ Laughter ]

00:07:09.567 --> 00:07:11.534
You know, on TikTok,

00:07:11.534 --> 00:07:15.501
you posted how you create
a beat for your song.

00:07:15.501 --> 00:07:17.367
And I thought it was very,
very cool and interesting.

00:07:17.367 --> 00:07:18.868
I wanted everyone to take
a look at this.

00:07:18.868 --> 00:07:23.634
This is Rosalía creating a beat
for her song "Saoko."

00:07:23.634 --> 00:07:25.367
-"Saoko."
-"Saoko."

00:07:25.367 --> 00:07:27.767
♪♪

00:07:27.767 --> 00:07:30.067
-[ Imitating melody ]

00:07:30.067 --> 00:07:32.701
♪♪

00:07:32.701 --> 00:07:35.000
[ Imitating melody ]

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:37.367
♪♪

00:07:37.367 --> 00:07:39.067
[ Vocalizing ]

00:07:39.067 --> 00:07:46.868
♪♪

00:07:46.868 --> 00:07:48.400
[ Laughter ]

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:50.501
-[ Imitating melody ]

00:07:50.501 --> 00:07:53.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:53.300 --> 00:07:56.601
That's so good.
-Jimmy, like the...

00:07:56.601 --> 00:07:58.634
-I love that.
Yeah, I love that.

00:07:58.634 --> 00:08:01.501
You're doing "Saturday Night
Live" this Saturday.

00:08:01.501 --> 00:08:03.100
-Yes.

00:08:03.100 --> 00:08:05.167
-Which, of course,
is on Saturday, and it's live.

00:08:05.167 --> 00:08:07.934
But you performed on "SNL"
with Bad Bunny,

00:08:07.934 --> 00:08:09.534
and you were amazing,
by the way.

00:08:09.534 --> 00:08:11.167
-Did you like it?
-I loved it.

00:08:11.167 --> 00:08:14.767
He's a pal, and I'm always --
I'm such a fan of yours.

00:08:14.767 --> 00:08:16.067
I'm so psyched to meet you

00:08:16.067 --> 00:08:17.634
and tell you in person
how much I love you.

00:08:17.634 --> 00:08:19.067
-Same.
-I can't wait to watch.

00:08:19.067 --> 00:08:20.901
Congrats on everything.
Please come back

00:08:20.901 --> 00:08:22.667
with more text messages.
-Yay.

00:08:22.667 --> 00:08:23.968
-Yeah. Just text me.

00:08:23.968 --> 00:08:25.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:25.501 --> 00:08:28.868
"Motomami" is out March 18th.
Rosalía, everybody.

00:08:28.868 --> 00:08:30.400
Check her out
as the musical guest

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:32.067
this weekend on
"Saturday Night Live."

00:08:32.067 --> 00:08:34.501
We'll be right back with
a performance from Omar Apollo.

00:08:34.501 --> 00:08:36.300
Stick around.

